# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env holds live Firebase and Cloudinary credentials. Despite its own header
# claiming "This file is gitignored", it was NOT listed here before Sprint 0.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Firebase Console downloads keys as <project>-firebase-adminsdk-<hash>.json,
# which matched none of the usual patterns. Broadened after one such key was
# found sitting unignored in the project root.
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
*-service-account*.json
*serviceAccountKey*.json
gcp-credentials*.json
*.credentials.json
secrets/
/.claude/
# ── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.*

# ── Next.js ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.next/
out/
build/
next-env.d.ts

# ── Testing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.vitest/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# ── Firebase ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.firebase/
firebase-debug.log
firestore-debug.log
ui-debug.log

# ── Misc ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.pem
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
# tesseract.js writes its ~5 MB language model beside the process that ran it.
# The browser caches its own copy, so this only ever appears when the OCR is
# driven from a node script.
*.traineddata
# ── Kept out of the repo by the project owner ─────────────────────────────
instruction.txt
# Defense preparation, not part of the system. Listed rather than merely left
# uncommitted because this repository is committed with `git add .`-style
# "update" commits, which would otherwise sweep them in unnoticed.
Questions.doc
Questions-Answered.doc
# Windows shortcuts hold absolute paths that mean nothing on another machine.
# create-internal-shortcut.bat regenerates them per machine.
*.lnk
# ── The client's own documents ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Moved to a PRIVATE repository:
#   https://github.com/anderson895/SFSR-REMS-Development-Guide
#
# The RBAC matrix, the employee roster, the reservation procedure and the
# company's bank and e-wallet details are St. Francis Square Realty's papers,
# not the project's, and none of them had to be world-readable for the code to
# be. The code still cites them by name and section — README §5.1 says how to
# put them back on disk.
#
# Ignored rather than merely removed, and the distinction matters here: this
# repository is committed with `git add .`-style "update" commits, exactly as
# the note above about Questions.doc says. Without this line the whole folder
# walks straight back into the next one.
Development_Guide/
